  "interpretation": [
    "The 4B BF16 result supports a conditional fresh-decode acceleration claim on this model, prompt suite, runtime, and machine.",
    "The 9B results fail the strict output-equivalence gate and remain experimental even where throughput improves.",
    "A reasoning prompt exceeds 2x on both BF16 targets, but the three-family medians remain near 1.6x.",
    "These results do not establish universal end-to-end speedup, semantic quality equivalence, sampling equivalence, or performance on unseen workloads.",
    "BF16 DFlash pairs use substantially more disk and unified memory than ordinary 4-bit native aliases."
